# Ignore rules for the Timeline TV add-on.
#
# Rule of thumb: only add-on sources, the build/test tooling that produces or
# verifies the XPI, and the documents that ship with it belong in this repository.
# Everything below is either generated, downloaded for local tooling, or scratch
# state belonging to one machine.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and release artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Produced by tools/package.mjs; rebuilt by CI and never edited by hand.
dist/
*.xpi
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Store/API credentials belong in .env on this machine and must never be
# committed. If a .env.example is ever added, it is explicitly allowed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling, not part of the add-on
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A locally unpacked GitHub CLI, if you used one to create the remote.
.gh/
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and scratch files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.tmp
*.bak
